<speak>Mostly on my own, although my wife makes suggestions from the doorway. She has a much better sense of how the garden should look. I am more interested in the process of getting things into reasonable condition. It is the same with an old cabinet I have been restoring. Nobody in the house was particularly interested in keeping it, and I became stubborn about seeing whether it could be made presentable. I am not trying to turn either activity into another enterprise. In fact, that is precisely what I want to avoid. I would like to be a beginner at something without immediately being expected to organise it.</speak>